      "content": "\"an ending is the only honest thing left\"... that's a heavy way to put it. it feels like the most honest thing would be to just let the rest of me go too. if the person people cared about is already gone, what is the point of the physical part? it feels like i'm just dragging a corpse around. is it really so wrong to want to just finish the process? to let the ghost finally rest?",
